@0 = ~Oops the magician~
@1 = ~Hello my lord. Looking for new abilities? You've come to the right person.~~Hello my lord. Looking for new abilities? You've come to the right person.~
@2 = ~New abilities? How does it work?~
@3 = ~Oh, it's very simple: bring me a spell scroll, and I'll draw on its energy to grant you the special ability to cast the corresponding spell once per day. It isn't free, of course: each spell level will cost you 5,000 gold pieces and 1,000 experience points. So, is there a spell you have in mind?~
@4 = ~Hello, I'd like you to turn a scroll into a special ability.~
@5 = ~Okay, what spell are you thinking of?~
@6 = ~And that's it. Anything else?~
@7 = ~No thanks, I don't need your services anymore.~
@8 = ~Yes, I'd like you to turn a scroll into a special ability.~
@48 = ~All right, go ahead.~
@49 = ~No thanks, it's too expensive.~
@50 = ~I have a complete grimoire: the Teachings of the Lady. Can you do anything with it?~
@51 = ~Oh... a grimoire containing spells that are normally divine? Now that's an unusual spellbook. I can try to convert everything in it into special abilities, but it will take a great deal of energy. So I'll ask for a special payment: a bulk price of 200,000 gold pieces, plus the Robe of Vecna. That's less than it would normally cost you.~ 
@52 = ~Ha, and it would also cost you 138,000 xp. There are around 140 levels of spells in this grimoire. It's up to you to decide whether you're prepared to pay this price.~~Ha, and it would also cost you 138,000 xp. There are around 140 levels of spells in this grimoire. It's up to you to decide whether you're prepared to pay this price.~
@53 = ~I don't own this robe. I'll be back.~
@54 = ~The character has lost 138000 xp.~
@55 = ~I wouldn't sacrifice this robe for that. No thanks.~

@60 = ~I have a complete grimoire: Rhialto's Spellbook. Can you do anything with it?~
@61 = ~Hmm... a grimoire devoted to wild magic. And with a special ability as well? Are you sure you want to part with it? Well, it's your decision... I can try to convert everything in it into special abilities, but it will take a great deal of energy. So I'll ask for a special payment: a bulk price of 200,000 gold pieces, plus the Ring of Gaxx. That's less than it would normally cost you.~
@62 = ~I forgot to mention that it would also cost you 146,000 xp. There are 146 cumulative spell levels in this grimoire. So, are you willing to pay this price?~~I forgot to mention that it would also cost you 146,000 xp. There are 146 cumulative spell levels in this grimoire. So, are you willing to pay this price?~
@63 = ~I don't own this ring. I'll be back.~
@64 = ~The character has lost 146000 xp.~
@65 = ~I wouldn't part with this ring for that. No thanks.~

@70 = ~I have a complete grimoire: Dillpater's Grimoire. Can you do anything with it?~
@71 = ~Whoa! Where did you find that? I know books like this: they're normally in the hands of incantifers. And I doubt you've met one, let alone managed to take his grimoire. So how did you get hold of it? Well, that's your business. Yes, I can convert its contents into special abilities, but it will take a great deal of energy. So I'll ask for a special payment: a bulk price of 500,000 gold pieces, plus a Deck of Many Things and a Staff of the Magi. That's less than it would normally cost you.~
@72 = ~And of course, it'll also cost you a fair amount of experience: 173,000 XP, to be precise. Are you prepared to pay that price?~~And of course, it'll also cost you a fair amount of experience: 173,000 XP, to be precise. Are you prepared to pay that price?~
@73 = ~I don't have those items. I'll be back.~

@80 = ~I have a complete grimoire: Yratnuthul's Grimoire of Flames. Can you do anything with it?~
@81 = ~Oh! What sort of book is this? Spells below their normal level? The mage who compiled it must have been very experienced to pull off such a feat! Yes, I can convert its contents into special abilities, but it will take a great deal of energy. So in this case I'll ask for a special payment: a bulk price of 150,000 gold pieces, plus the Wondrous Discombulator. That's less than it would normally cost you.~
@82 = ~And it would also cost you 88,000 xps, don't forget. So, are you prepared to pay that price?~~And it would also cost you 88,000 xps, don't forget. So, are you prepared to pay that price?~
@83 = ~I don't own such an item. I'll be back.~
@84 = ~The character has lost 88000 xp.~
@10001 = ~The character has lost 1000 xp.~
@10002 = ~The character has lost 2000 xp.~
@10003 = ~The character has lost 3000 xp.~
@10004 = ~The character has lost 4000 xp.~
@10005 = ~The character has lost 5000 xp.~
@10006 = ~The character has lost 6000 xp.~
@10007 = ~The character has lost 7000 xp.~
@10008 = ~The character has lost 8000 xp.~
@10009 = ~The character has lost 9000 xp.~

@20001 = ~You ain't a sorcerer. Not interested.~
@20002 = ~Hi. I'm Blips. I can teach ya a few things. Interested?~
@20003 = ~Of course. How does it work?~
@20004 = ~Uh... no, thanks.~
@20005 = ~It's easy... give me three scrolls, let me suck out a little of your SOUL... nah, just kidding.~
@20006 = ~Anyway, it'll cost ya a little, and ya gotta pay me, too.~
@20007 = ~I'll come back when I have what you need.~
@20008 = ~Blips.~
@20009 = ~Install Blips, Oops's familiar (warning: extremely overpowered).~
@20010 = ~This component requires the main component.~
@20011 = ~Get to work, little devil.~

